  "description": "The third term of the validation guard, app/cbl/COMEN01C.cbl:129 - WS-OPTION = ZEROS - reached with a blank OPTIONI. The descending test-before scan at 117-121 stops at WS-IDX 1 because byte two is a space, line 122 sends one byte into the PIC X(02) JUST RIGHT receiver, and line 123's INSPECT REPLACING ALL ' ' BY '0' turns '  ' into '00' - so the operator who pressed ENTER on an empty field is rejected by the ZEROS term rather than by IS NOT NUMERIC. The rejected value is still echoed to OPTIONO by line 125, normalised to '00'. The ungated filter at 136-137 then subscripts the table with 0, which is BELOW the OCCURS range and which COBOL has no subscript for at all; the bounded read yields nothing and the filter is false, so exactly one screen is painted.",
